  "narration": {
    "title": "The Arms That End Innings Clean",
    "intro": "The best relievers don't pile up numbers; they pile up quiet nights. Today we rank the season's elite bullpen arms by our form score, the ones who walk in and walk off without a scratch. The names at the top are doing it with a regularity that borders on boring.",
    "relievers_lead": "Mason Miller sits at a perfect form of 100, and the line is almost unfair: a 0.79 ERA, a matching 0.79 WHIP, 21 saves and 66 strikeouts, with a clean outing in 94 percent of his 32 appearances and every one of his seven inherited runners stranded. Dylan Lee shares that 100 with a different job, 15 holds and a 0.63 WHIP for the Braves, and he hasn't allowed an earned run in his last nine innings. What ties this board together is consistency over volume, and Louis Varland is the proof, a 0.84 ERA and 16 saves in Toronto from a man whose career form sits at 53, this year the leverage finally his to keep."
  }
}